ituation but yeah I thought John  Bradley did a great job here and it  really was one of my favorite parts of  the episode I think we kind of see in  Daenerys his face here how she struggles  she wants to be compassionate but at the  same time she can't change what she did  so I think her reaction to Sam was  pretty spot-on and that she's the queen  here this is an interaction between the  Queen and someone not to regular people  just having a chat doesn't make it any  easier for Sam and it doesn't make it  any easier for us as viewers to watch  him have to deal with this then we see  him go outside and he runs into bran who  says he's waiting for an old friend  and then he drops it on Sam that he has  to go tell Jon right now basically that  Ned isn't his father of course this  leads us into the big reveal as Sam goes  and finds John in the crypts it happened  kind of fast for me in that I wasn't  expecting Sam to be so forceful in the  way he delivered this because he just  heard about his brother and his father  that played a big part in it so yeah it  was interesting the first time I watched  I was like John didn't even really bring  up the idea that he's dating his aunt  but I kind of see how they went with it  as far as you know Ned was the most  honorable man he ever knew that's the  guy he looked up to all his life I read  the interview with kid Harrington when  he was talking about it he said that you  know Sam is nothing tomb in that moment  because this is so much of a shake to  his foundation telling him that Ned had  lied John says that you know he would  beat Sam up and disown him forever if he  found out that he was playing with him  on this level like if he was playing  with his emotions about something this  important the way what's important here  is Sam delivered the information perhaps  later on John will be like oh yeah I did  write a dragon maybe that's why but I  don't think there's any doubt left in  John by the time this wraps up and I  think that was what was important as far  as what had to happen he's gonna have a  period of time where he adjusts to the  idea he's gonna have to figure out what  it all means and he's gonna have to talk  to his partner here Daenerys and figure  out how that all shakes out starting  from Daenerys is revealed to Sam it's a  turn in the episode to where things get  pretty grave Don has to struggle with  this then we go up north a bit into the  last hearth and we see what happened to  Ned umber when I thought about this  episode beforehand and how everything  was pretty laid out I imagine there had  to be something to remind us of the  threat of course most of us who pay so  much attention we don't need a reminder  but you know casual fans might not be  sitting around at night charting where  they think the night Kings going or what  he wants and things like that so this  was our reminder that something's going  on and it's all headed towards  Winterfell it was kind of shocking the  symbolism was pretty strong as far as  using that swirl again  my head Canon on this for a long time  has been that ever since we saw the  children of the forest create the night  king in that location that swirl is  repeated in a lot of different things  that we see so my head cannons kind of  evolved to the thing of like this is  something that they know this is  something that is kind of a universal  symbol of where he came from it's a  reminder in a way of what they are a lot  of people pointed out the fact that it  looked like the Targaryen sigil kinda  when it was on fire and it did but I  don't know if that's what we were  supposed to take away from that at all  but either way there was a bit of horror  there berrak just says it right out this  is a message from the knight  like he knows what's going on it seemed  a little bit weird to me at the time but  yeah that's it works fine I guess then  we head back to Winterfell and we see  Jamie arrive and we see him spot bran  and we made the connection that bran has  been sitting there for a whole day more  or less like through the night into the  next day waiting for Jamie to arrive I'm  not a hundred percent convinced that  that's who he was waiting for but either  way we get this reunion which was the  one I was most interested to see  honestly and it's a pretty well acted  seeing there we see that there's  recognition from bran that hey there's  Jamie Lannister and we see Jamie sort of  shuffle through emotions in his head  before he arrives on the last bit of  like oh man you know this guy probably  wants revenge against me at least that's  what the actor described it as and I  think it came off pretty well the  question of whether bran is there  waiting for him or for someone else is a  natural question to ask I think if he is  waiting for Jamie then why would he be  specifically waiting for him if he's not  waiting for Jamie then who would he be  waiting for and that is where the  episode ends episode 1 of season 8 ends  the same way as episode 1 of season 1  does an interaction between Jamie and  bran and a fade to black so yeah I think  that you know there are some interesting  things here there was also a lot of  pushing stories along to get things to  where they needed to be I didn't love  the episode but I didn't hate it there  were things I loved in it and there were  things that I kind of hated in it I do  however accept it in order to have  payoffs later we have to have setups now  I think things are gonna get dark real  quick so I think it's okay to have a  little bit of fun with things for them  in the beginning some of the things I  found promising I liked that we saw a  little bit of humanity under the surface  of Arya and bran I think bran is gonna  play a really big part in preparing for  the battle and I think that he has a  unique role I mean obviously Jon and  Daenerys have their roles but I think he  has a unique role and actually defeating  the night king so I find it really  interesting to see who he's waiting for  and why  he's waiting for them I think he is  going to end up having a plan I do tend  to believe that that's who the night  king is after when he says he has a  target so I think bran would be able to  use that to his advantage and possibly  set a trap or do something to even  things up because the night King has a  huge advantage here it was a quick look  at Tyrion that was interesting that bran  made - I thought Tyrion had kind of a  weird episode I didn't think that he  really fit anywhere with any people I  mean he obviously was comfortable with  Varys and Davos talking about a marriage  proposal but I thought it was  interesting that we opened with him in  Varys but then we really didn't see them  playing a big effective role in anything  going on as far as the South is  concerned I think that it's pretty clear  that Cersei has lost her pregnancy most  of us expected that to happen it was  mentioned in the leaks that turned out  to be pretty accurate for Season seven  that there would be a scene where she  lost the child we never saw that  on-screen but it's also foreshadowed  there that Euron will not necessarily go  down with her if it turns out to be a  situation where they're gonna lose for  sure he says a tiara if he's fighting  for the wrong side then he'll take his  iron fleet and go somewhere else the  bran stuff is interesting but I'm not  sure how it figures into the endgame at  this point at least not what's in front  of them right now there's quite a lot of  foreshadowing I expect that since they  cut off John's talk with Sam about his  parentage and they cut off the reunion  between bran and Jaime that will pick  right up with those things and figure  out what's going on there I don't think  they'll leave those hanging I think  Jon's gonna have to reckon with that and  there's going to be a lot of other stuff  going on so there's going to be a lot of  tension leading up to the preparation I  expected that Tyrion would play a bigger  role but now he looks like he's kind of  being isolated in a way that's probably  foreshadowing about how things are gonna  go for him if bran was waiting for Jaime  then that's foreshadowing that he has  some big part to play in the battle for  Winterfell the ritualistic display of  Ned umbers body in the way this thing  went up in flames really kind of him  at what the night king is up to what he  wants and that would really take a lot  more explaining from my point of view so  I'll leave that there at this point I'm  certainly interested to see how things  will play out next time I made a trailer  breakdown for the second episode which I  think is going to be the preparation  episode because we know episode 3 is  going to be the Battle episode so you  can check that out there are several  different little bonus videos I'd like  to make related to this it's just gonna  be a question of whether I have the time  to do that this week or not so please  check back please like this video if you  enjoyed it please subscribe to my  channel and thanks for watching I'll  talk to you soon  you
 

